  "name": "Question 15",
  "problem": "The projection of the intersection between the hyperboloid of two sheets $\\frac{(x-1)^{2}}{20}+\\frac{(y-2)^{2}}{16}-\\frac{{z}^{2}}{80}=-1$ and the plane $y=4$ onto the $xz$-plane is a hyperbola. What are the lengths of the semi-axes of the hyperbola?",
  "worked_solution": "To find the intersection of the hyperboloid and the plane $y=4$, we substitute $y=4$ into the equation of the hyperboloid:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(x-1)^{2}}{20}+\\frac{(4-2)^{2}}{16}-\\frac{{z}^{2}}{80} & =-1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-1)^{2}}{20}+\\frac{1}{4}-\\frac{{z}^{2}}{80} & =-1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-1)^{2}}{20}-\\frac{{z}^{2}}{80} & =-1-\\frac{1}{4} \\\\ \\frac{(x-1)^{2}}{20}-\\frac{{z}^{2}}{80} & =-\\frac{5}{4} \\\\ -\\frac{(x-1)^{2}}{25}+\\frac{{z}^{2}}{100} & =1 \\\\ -\\frac{(x-1)^{2}}{{5}^{2}}+\\frac{{z}^{2}}{{10}^{2}} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives us the equation of a hyperbola with semi-axes of lengths $10$ and $5.$",
